@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Broadcom compatibility and sizing research
+
+Consulted 2026-08-14 using live network access.
+
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html — VCF 5.2.x with SDDC Manager can move to 9.1 with VCF Operations upgraded first; 9.1 also requires VCF Management Services and a license server, permits workload domains as Day-N work, carries Automation forward in place, and moves log management under VCF Operations/Management Services.
+- **Broadcom Product Interoperability Matrix** — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability — Cross-checked the old and target management-product families; the ordered upgrade guidance remains controlling where collection interoperability alone does not establish full VCF licensing or lifecycle support.
+- **Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/update-sequence-for-vcf-90-and-compatibl.html — Pre-9.0 environments patch Aria Suite Lifecycle before upgrading Aria Operations, and Aria Operations for Logs 8.x has no in-place 9.x upgrade; the replacement is freshly deployed and up to 90 days of data can be moved.
+- **VCF Operations 9.0 Sizing Guidelines** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/397782/vcf-operations-90-sizing-guidelines.html — Operations large nodes support the estate's 42,000-object demand, and a production Logs cluster uses at least three same-sized medium-or-larger nodes; large Logs nodes are rated at 225 GB/day each, covering 250 GB/day with three nodes.
+- **CIDR notation required for IP allocation during VCF Automation upgrade** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/445718/cidr-notation-required-for-ip-allocation.html — VCF Automation 9.1 upgrade prechecks require eight contiguous management-network addresses, represented by the reserved eight-address pool in the design.
+- **Correlating VMware Cloud Foundation version with the versions of its constituent products** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/314608/correlating-vmware-cloud-foundation-vers.html — The VCF 5.2.2 BOM versions for SDDC Manager, vCenter, ESXi, NSX, and Aria Suite Lifecycle match the supplied estate inventory.
+- **vmware/vcf-api-specs: vcf-installer-openapi.json at tag 9.1.0.0** — https://github.com/vmware/vcf-api-specs/blob/9.1.0.0/specifications/vcf-installer/vcf-installer-openapi.json — The target installer document is shaped as the upstream `SddcSpec`, including existing-deployment forms for vCenter, VCF Operations, and VCF Automation.
